UPDATE "lessons" AS l SET "summary" = 'Build forms people can use, including people with disabilities.', "body" = 'Forms let visitors send you information. Accessible forms work for everyone, including people using screen readers or only a keyboard.

```
<form action="https://formspree.io/f/your-id" method="post">
  <label for="name">Your name</label>
  <input id="name" name="name" required>

  <label for="phone">Phone number</label>
  <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel">

  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>
```

### Rules that help everyone
- Every input needs a `<label>` linked with `for` and `id`.
- Use the right input **type** (`tel`, `email`, `number`) so phones show the right keyboard.
- Make buttons big enough to tap: at least 44 pixels high.
- Use strong colour contrast between text and background.
- Make sure everything works with the keyboard alone (Tab and Enter).

A form on a static site needs a service to receive the messages, such as a free form service.

Draft lesson: to be checked by a JesTech subject reviewer before launch.', "checklist" = '["Build a form with labelled inputs","Use tel or email input types","Check you can use it with the keyboard only"]'::jsonb, "est_minutes" = 12
